VLLM cache multi-modal outputs from HuggingFace processors for performance reasons. The model's processor is responsible for processing the input data and generating output, which can be used in multiple modalities by passing it through different models or preprocessors.
The cache helps to avoid re-processing past multi-modal inputs, as each API process uses a unique set of arguments that are passed from one step to another. This reduces memory usage and improves performance for certain use cases where the model needs to handle large amounts of data in multiple modalities at once.
Additionally, vLLM caches non-default pooling config or default pooling config for thePooling model, which can help improve overall system efficiency by reducing the amount of computation required when processing a single input.
